[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139645,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteoblastoma is a locally aggressive bone-forming tumour, generally &gt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;mm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139646,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9200/1 Osteoblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139647,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E83.Z &amp; XH4316 Benign osteogenic tumour of unspecified site &amp; Osteoblastoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139648,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> epithelioid osteoblastoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> pseudomalignant osteoblastoma; aggressive osteoblastoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139649,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139650,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In more than one&nbsp;third of cases the spine is affected. The craniofacial bones, including the orbit, are affected in &lt;&nbsp;5% of cases {33049284;17052641;24256752}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139651,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The presenting symptom is frequently pain and/or swelling {8119712;33049284}. In the orbit, this may include exophthalmos, hearing or visual loss, diplopia, and nasal obstruction {24256752;33049284}.</p>\r\n<p>On radiographs and CT, osteoblastomas present as lytic lesions &gt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;mm, frequently with surrounding reactive sclerosis {27476846}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139652,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteoblastomas represent &lt;&nbsp;1% of primary bone tumours {18561158;8119712}. The peak incidence is between the second and third decades of life. In general, the M:F&nbsp;ratio is 2:1 {18561158;8119712}; however, in the orbit the reported sex distribution is equal {33049284}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139653,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139654,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Rearrangement of <em>FOS</em> is present in 87% of osteoblastomas {29858576;30582658}, and in a smaller percentage of cases <em>FOSB</em> rearrangement has been detected {29858576}. <em>FOS</em> rearrangements can be detected using an antibody against the FOS N-terminus, which results in nuclear immunoreactivity in the osteoblastic cells {30582658;31490237;31768625}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139655,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139656,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteoblastomas are characterized by interconnecting, delicate, woven bone trabeculae, rimmed by a single layer of polygonal osteoblasts {8119712}. The stroma is loose and usually richly vascularized, with dilated capillary-type blood vessels. Destructive host bone permeation and atypical mitotic figures should not be seen. The differential diagnosis includes sino-orbital osteoma with osteoblastoma-like features.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139657,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139658,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>FOS</em> gene rearrangement or rarely <em>FOSB</em> gene rearrangement is found in the majority of osteoblastomas {29858576}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139659,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> bone-forming tumour composed of trabeculae of woven bone rimmed by plump osteoblasts in a vascularized stroma; absence of host bone permeation; compatible radiological features of a &gt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;mm lesion with well-defined tumour borders.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139660,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139661,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 285,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis is good, but recurrences are described in as many as 23% of cases {18561158}, more frequently in patients in which complete excision has not been achieved, and this can be challenging at this location {18561158}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]